WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:01.960
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.370
- A lot of the work you do is with blocks.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.223
It's the core shape of the platform.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.250
- [Narrator] Samuel Jordan
has been making video games

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.280
since he was 15 years old.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.490
- I've gone from making clothing stores

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.350
to 3D cafes and food restaurants

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.130
to now full-fledged games.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.110
- [Narrator] He's made all of these

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.170
on a free online gaming
platform called Roblox,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.720
which is available on
Desktop, mobile devices

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.820
and Xbox consoles.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.660
Last year, at the age of 21,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.513
Jordan earned more than $600,000.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.920
- Not yet.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.330
- [Narrator] He's among the
seven million Roblox developers

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.010
who've built the company a library

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.900
of over 20 million games and experiences.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.270
And this has attracted
about 33 million daily users

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.690
and more than half of them
are under the age of 13.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.171
The pandemic fueled this model

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:51.880
and Roblox became a place

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.780
where kids at home could hang out.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.340
This has made it one of the
valuable video game companies

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.330
in the world.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.270
And its first day of trading in March,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.993
saw a market valuation of $45 billion.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.200
But as new games are created every day,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.640
the company faces the challenge

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.410
of moderating its platform.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.730
And its business model rides

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.990
on whether Roblox can remain
a safe place for kids.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.450
- My daughter's obsessed with Roblox.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.960
I know this platform way too well.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.487
She loves "Royale High."

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.930
- [Narrator] Sarah Needleman
covers the video game industry

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.300
for The Wall Street Journal

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.500
and she's been spending
a lot of time on Roblox

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.400
with her daughter.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.030
- Got this yesterday.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.140
- [Narrator] An even owns a copy

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.810
of "The Ultimate Guide to Roblox."

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.710
- All of the games on the platform

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.570
have been made by users.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.000
Some are just individuals like you and I

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.190
but the company itself
doesn't make the games

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.453
that are on the platform.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.040
- [Narrator] This means
Roblox doesn't have to rely

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.340
on Hollywood-like budgets

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.420
and rockstar talent to
produce blockbuster titles.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.730
For example, one of last year's
most anticipated video games

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.810
was "Cyberpunk 2077,"

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.580
a game that cost Polish company CD Projekt

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.260
more than $300 million

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.760
to develop and market.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.420
Just compare that with Roblox,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.480
which provides a free developer toolkit

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.600
for anyone interested in
creating content for it.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.270
- Luckily, Roblox has a lot
of these pre-made for us,

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.220
so we're just gonna go into
our toolbox and find one.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.960
- You don't have to be an expert in coding

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.610
to make games for Roblox.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.520
There are step-by-step resources

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.120
and a lot of it's drag and drop.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.990
Somewhat turnkey you could say.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.790
So that has made it very
attractive to younger folks

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.740
who are just learning
how to do this stuff.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.573
- [Narrator] Roblox says

00:02:29.573 --> 00:02:31.540
it's continually updating the toolkit.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.870
This helps developers
make engaging content

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.010
so its players don't get bored.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.210
- They can make higher-equality games

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.400
and the kind of games that adults

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.310
would appreciate more so than youngsters.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.640
They're more complicated,
they're more challenging.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.950
- [Narrator] This creates an ecosystem

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.400
of players and developers.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.710
Just look at Samuel Jordan.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.410
- It felt just really inspiring

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:54.560
to think wow, at a young
age, I can make something.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.470
- [Narrator] He first
started playing in 2011

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.490
and four years later,

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.060
he began creating his own
worlds, like Fairytale.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.360
- Yay, a new friend.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.010
- [Narrator] Today he's
building complex games

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.180
for young children

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.670
and even took a break from college

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.660
during the pandemic to focus on Roblox

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.250
with his friends.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.230
Jordan was also hand picked by the company

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.520
when he was 19 years old

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.280
to help expand the toolkit.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.770
- They've also increased the amount

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.090
of textures you can add in game

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.860
and it's really helped to
really build an atmosphere

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.050
for your games.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.030
- [Narrator] Games are
free to play on Roblox.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.770
So Jordan only starts to earn money

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:31.350
when a player spends the
in-game currency called Robux.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.390
- [Samuel] Earning money on Roblox

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.970
is actually a pretty easy process.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.460
People will pay you with Robux

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.650
and you can exchange those out for dollars

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.390
or your local currency.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:40.770
- [Narrator] So players
can link their accounts

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.830
to credit cards and for young children,

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.660
they can use prepaid gift cards.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.900
With Robux, they can
buy this Prince jacket

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.761
or pay for a pass to
visit the Dream Mansion.

00:03:50.761 --> 00:03:52.750
(pensive music)

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.770
Jordan also makes money from
collaborations with brands,

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.180
turning real-world products

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.730
into Roblox items

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.070
but he doesn't get to keep all the money.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.740
Developers receive 70%

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.700
of the Robux spent in their games

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.690
and get 30% of the Robux spent

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.930
on items they put up for sale.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.270
Roblox says the rest goes
to running the business,

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.773
including hosting services and operations.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.640
As players flocked to
Roblox during the pandemic,

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.120
the company said its
revenue last year grew 82%,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.330
while sales of virtual
items more than doubled

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.563
to about $2 billion.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.990
But user loyalty hasn't
translated into profits.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.000
The company has incurred net losses

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.400
since its inception in 2004.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:37.670
And last year, those losses
exceeded $250 million,

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.973
in part because of higher operating costs.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.450
But profitability isn't
the only challenge.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.740
There's been an increasing amount

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.810
of adult content on some games.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:48.970
- All the sort of bad actors
you see on social media,

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:52.300
you would have to assume could
happen on a site like Roblox.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.750
The only difference is that Roblox happens

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:56.120
to appeal to a very young audience.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.210
Probably youngsters are more sort

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.110
to bad actors than adults maybe

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.120
and so it raises the bar
in terms of moderation.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.070
- [Narrator] Roblox said it hired

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.710
more than 2,300 content moderators

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.220
while inappropriate words
are replaced with hashtags.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.100
The company also said it's now developing

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.870
content ratings for games

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.404
and making parental controls
easier to find and use.

00:05:19.404 --> 00:05:20.560
(upbeat music)

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.261
But as countries emerge from the pandemic,

00:05:22.261 --> 00:05:25.210
Roblox hopes the habits
of using the platform

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.950
aren't easy to break.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:30.020
Even Jordan says he'll continue to create.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.820
- I don't think I'm gonna
be chasing to keep people on

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.690
past the pandemic.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.270
I'm gonna continue to make content

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.930
I think players will enjoy

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.060
and the ones that stay long

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.041
are gonna be there 'cause they
enjoy the time they spend.

00:05:41.041 --> 00:05:43.071
(lively music)

